And some things are more valuable because we do. ;)

Not everything meaningful needs to be expressed, shared, explained, demonstrated, or understood by someone else.

Some experiences belong to us. Some discoveries need privacy to mature. Some joys are best enjoyed without an audience.

There is a difference between secrecy, privacy, intimacy, and sovereignty.

And there’s power in knowing that difference.

You can be transparent without being exposed. Generous without giving everything away. Intimate without surrendering your individuality.

Even in love, two people don’t have to become one indistinguishable thing. Sometimes the space between them is what allows the relationship to breathe.

Knowing what to share is wisdom. Knowing what to preserve is wisdom too.

And perhaps there’s another kind of ripening here: reaching a point where you no longer need everyone else to witness something for it to feel real.

Some things we give away.

Some things we grow together.

And some things we keep because they’re ours. ;)